==French==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|fr|gem-pro|ine-pro}}
{{inh+|fr|frm|laisser}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|lesser}}, {{m|fro|lessier}}, {{m|fro|laissier||to let, let go, leave}}, from {{inh|fr|la|laxō|laxāre|to relax, loosen}}; possibly partly from or influenced by {{der|fr|goh|lāzan||to let, let go, leave}} ({{cog|de|lassen}}), from {{der|fr|gmw-pro|*lātan||to let, leave, leave alone}}. More at {{m|en|let}}, {{m|en|lay}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|ang|lǣtan||to allow, let go, leave, rent}}, {{cog|got|𐌻𐌴𐍄𐌰𐌽||to release, forgive}}, {{cog|it|lasciare||to leave, let, allow}}. Conflated also with {{cog|fro|laiier||to leave, abandon, allow}} (compare {{cog|pro|laihar}}, {{m|pro|laiar}}, Old Northern {{cog|it|lagare}}), also of {{cog|gem}} origin, from {{cog|got|𐌻𐌰𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽||to lay, let lie, leave}}, from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*lagjaną||to lay}}.
{{col-bottom}}

